# AI Context Rules - Next.js Frontend Project

## Tech Stack
- **Framework:** Next.js 16.2.2 (App Router)
- **Language:** Strict TypeScript
- **UI:** React 19.2.4, Tailwind CSS 4
- **Components:** shadcn/ui v4
- **Icons:** Lucide React

## Architecture & Design Patterns

### Clean Architecture (Frontend)
```
src/
├── app/                    # Next.js pages & layouts (route-based)
├── components/            # Reusable UI components
│   ├── ui/               # shadcn primitives
│   └── features/         # Feature-specific components
├── lib/                   # Utilities, configs, helpers
├── services/              # API calls, external integrations
├── hooks/                 # Custom React hooks (business logic)
├── types/                 # TypeScript interfaces & DTOs
└── store/                 # State management (if needed)
```

### Separation of Concerns
- **Components:** Pure UI rendering, receive data via props
- **Hooks:** Encapsulate business logic, state management
- **Services:** Handle API communication, data fetching
- **Types:** Define data shapes (DTOs), no implementation

## Data Handling & TypeScript

### DTOs & Types
- Define interfaces for all API responses and request payloads
- Use `readonly` for immutable data structures
- Never expose raw API responses directly to components; map to component-specific types
- Use discriminated unions for variant types

### Validation
- Zod for runtime validation (Next.js preferred over class-validator)
- Validate at service/hook boundary, not in components

## Naming Conventions
- **Files:** `kebab-case` (e.g., `user-profile.tsx`, `use-user-profile.ts`)
- **Components:** `PascalCase` (e.g., `UserProfile.tsx`)
- **Hooks:** `camelCase` with `use` prefix (e.g., `useUserProfile`)
- **Types/Interfaces:** `PascalCase` (e.g., `UserProfileDto`)
- **Constants:** `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`

## Component Patterns

### File Organization
- One component per file
- Colocate tests, stories, and types with component
- Use index exports for cleaner imports

### Component Structure
```typescript
// types/component-name.ts
interface ComponentNameProps { ... }

// components/component-name.tsx
export function ComponentName(props: ComponentNameProps) { ... }
```

## Token Optimization Rules

### Output Guidelines
- Output only the requested code or modified files
- Skip setup explanations unless explicitly asked
- Use absolute imports from `@/` alias (configured in tsconfig.json)
- No conversational filler or redundant explanations
- Assume developer expertise

### Import Conventions
```typescript
// Preferred
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button';
import { useUserProfile } from '@/hooks/use-user-profile';

// Avoid relative paths for project imports
```

## Code Quality
- Enable strict TypeScript (`strict: true` in tsconfig)
- No `any` types - use `unknown` with proper type guards
- ESLint + Prettier for formatting
- Run `npm run lint` before commits

## Environment
- Use `.env.local` for local secrets
- Never commit secrets to version control